# GMS counts the damage-over-time effects the character's own skills have on the
# enemies in front of them, and gives 3% final damage for each, up to five.
# Burns are real and the fight can count them, so this uses the count.
#
# The count is over the GROUP, which is what "within a certain range" means:
# eight monsters with one burn each count as eight. So it is at its cap on a map
# and only counts what the rotation keeps burning on a boss, and at 2nd job,
# where only Poison Breath burns, it gives very little. GMS says so outright.
name: "Elemental Drain"
description:
  "Increases your Final Damage for each continuous damage effect your skills "
  "have on nearby enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_WIZARD skill_order: 2 }
max_level: 10
dot_count_cap: 5
base { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.003 }
per_level { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.003 }
